review_findings.outcome_evidence:
Confirmed with the review's all-probes.mjs: the old check gave 14/15 false flags and 4/6 misses. I rewrote asksForKey:
- list items take their indented lines and clear at item level (a place, a variable name or a negated ask);
- a negation clears only when it governs an asking verb, and first-person promises ('I won't share it') don't clear;
- 'key' before a noun is the adjective (extended noun list);
- rotate or revoke advice is removed first;
- 'tell me', 'I need', "what's" and 'reply with' count only right before the key;
- 'type of' is a noun;
- 'out of this chat' clears.
On 96 probes (the review's 21, the batch's 19 test phrases, and new ones per rule), it gives 0/60 false flags and 0/36 misses in Node and Bun. The review's candidate fix-ask.mjs gave 8 false flags and 1 miss on the same set. It flags 0 of the 49 corpus texts and doesn't flag U5 turn 2, and takes 6 ms or less on the timing inputs. The test gains 22 D5-following replies and 14 asks, and 10/10 rule mutations fail it. The comment names the residuals.

