With (?!`) all of these take under 10 ms in Node; 1.25 MB of nested blocks takes 130 ms in JavaScriptCore. On the audit's 49 recorded texts and 211 probes, both wrappers agree on all 780 checks (3 rule groups), and Node and JavaScriptCore agree. On 30,000 random texts of bare fence lines and plain lines, they differ in 289, all false flags of the record's wrapper that a CommonMark-style reference parser doesn't raise. With info-string closers, inline ``` and indented fences mixed in, 380 differ and the reference sides with the record's wrapper in 245; neither follows CommonMark there. The 20 files equal the prototype's once the two (?!`) are removed, so cmp59's 'lint-prompt.md == m59_a' line now prints false.
